class":87},[60,707,709,712,715,718],{"class":62,"line":708},21,[60,710,711],{"class":66},"    return",[60,713,714],{"class":66}," &",[60,716,717],{"class":87},"u, ",[60,719,720],{"class":152},"nil\n",[60,722,724],{"class":62,"line":723},22,[60,725,236],{"class":87},[28,727,729],{"id":728},"_8-worker-pool-concurrency","8. Worker Pool (concurrency)",[14,731,732,733,736],{},"Implement a worker pool: N workers process jobs from a channel, write results to another. Use ",[18,734,735],{},"sync.WaitGroup",". Test with 1000 jobs and 10 workers.",[28,738,740],{"id":739},"_9-pipeline-concurrency","9. Pipeline (concurrency)",[14,742,743,744,254],{},"Build a 3-stage pipeline: generate numbers → square → filter evens. Print results. Add cancellation via ",[18,745,746],{},"context",[28,748,750],{"id":749},"_10-file-processor-io","10. File Processor (I\u002FO)",[14,752,753,754,247,757,247,760,763],{},"Read a CSV file, process each row, write a JSON file. Use ",[18,755,756],{},"encoding\u002Fcsv",[18,758,759],{},"encoding\u002Fjson",[18,761,762],{},"bufio",". Handle errors at each step.",[28,765,767],{"id":766},"_11-custom-error-type-error-handling","11. Custom Error Type (error handling)",[14,769,770,771,774,775,324,778,781,782,785,786,789],{},"Define a ",[18,772,773],{},"ValidationError"," with ",[18,776,777],{},"Field",[18,779,780],{},"Message",". Implement ",[18,783,784],{},"Error()",". Use ",[18,787,788],{},"errors.As"," to extract it in a caller.",[28,791,793],{"id":792},"_12-benchmark-a-function-testing","12. Benchmark a Function (testing)",[14,795,796,797,324,800,803,804,807,808,254],{},"Write a function and a benchmark. Measure ",[18,798,799],{},"ns\u002Fop",[18,801,802],{},"allocs\u002Fop",". Optimize to reduce allocations (pre-size, ",[18,805,806],{},"strings.Builder","). Compare before\u002Fafter with ",[18,809,810],{},"benchstat",[23,812,814],{"id":813},"advanced","Advanced",[28,816,818],{"id":817},"_13-concurrent-web-crawler-concurrency-context","13. Concurrent Web Crawler (concurrency, context)",[14,820,821,822,824,825,828],{},"Crawl a website concurrently: fetch a page, extract links, crawl each (bounded by a worker pool). Limit depth, respect ",[18,823,746],{}," cancellation, avoid revisiting URLs (",[18,826,827],{},"sync.Map"," or a mutex-protected map).",[28,830,832],{"id":831},"_14-job-queue-with-retry-concurrency-errors","14. Job Queue with Retry (concurrency, errors)",[14,834,835,836,838],{},"Build a job queue where failed jobs retry with exponential backoff. Use ",[18,837,746],{}," for cancellation. Track job state (pending, running, done, failed).",[28,840,842],{"id":841},"_15-rate-limited-api-client-rate-limiting","15. Rate-Limited API Client (rate limiting)",[14,844,845,846,849],{},"Use ",[18,847,848],{},"golang.org\u002Fx\u002Ftime\u002Frate"," to rate-limit API calls to 10\u002Fsecond with a burst of 5. Test with 100 calls and verify timing.",[28,851,853],{"id":852},"_16-in-memory-cache-sync-generics","16. In-Memory Cache (sync, generics)",[14,855,320,856,859,860,863],{},[18,857,858],{},"Cache[K, V]"," with TTL (time-to-live). Use ",[18,861,862],{},"sync.RWMutex"," for concurrent access. Expire entries in the background.",[28,865,867],{"id":866},"_17-http-server-with-middleware-interfaces-http","17. HTTP Server with Middleware (interfaces, http)",[14,869,870,871,874,875,254],{},"Build an HTTP server with middleware: logging, authentication, request ID. Use ",[18,872,873],{},"context.WithValue"," for request-scoped data. Test with ",[18,876,877],{},"httptest",[28,879,881],{"id":880},"_18-database-app-databasesql","18. Database App (database\u002Fsql)",[14,883,884,885,38,888,891,892,894,895,774,898,901,902,309],{},"Build a CRUD app with ",[18,886,887],{},"database\u002Fsql",[18,889,890],{},"pgx","). Use ",[18,893,746],{}," for query cancellation. Handle ",[18,896,897],{},"sql.ErrNoRows",[18,899,900],{},"errors.Is",". Write tests with a real database (or ",[18,903,904],{},"sqlmock",[23,906,908],{"id":907},"pro-capstone","Pro \u002F Capstone",[28,910,912],{"id":911},"_19-distributed-task-system-concurrency-context-error-handling","19. Distributed Task System (concurrency, context, error handling)",[14,914,915],{},"Build a task system: submit tasks to a queue, workers process them with retries, results stored. Features: priority queues, deadlines, graceful shutdown, metrics.",[28,917,919],{"id":918},"_20-chat-server-concurrency-networking","20. Chat Server (concurrency, networking)",[14,921,922,923,925],{},"Build a TCP chat server: clients connect, broadcast messages to all connected clients. Use goroutines per connection, channels for message passing, ",[18,924,827],{}," for client registry. Handle disconnects and graceful shutdown.",[28,927,929],{"id":928},"_21-url-shortener-http-database-caching","21. URL Shortener (HTTP, database, caching)",[14,931,932],{},"Build a URL shortener: short codes redirect to long URLs. Use a database for persistence, an in-memory cache for hot URLs, and a hash function for short codes. Add analytics (click counts) and expiration.",[28,934,936],{"id":935},"_22-file-sync-tool-io-concurrency","22. File Sync Tool (I\u002FO, concurrency)",[14,938,939,940,942,943,309],{},"Build a tool that syncs two directories: detect changes (mtime\u002Fhash), copy\u002Fupdate\u002Fdelete. Use goroutines for parallel file hashing, ",[18,941,746],{}," for cancellation. Handle large files by streaming (",[18,944,945],{},"io.Copy",[28,947,949],{"id":948},"_23-pubsub-system-concurrency-channels","23. Pub\u002FSub System (concurrency, channels)",[14,951,952,953,955],{},"Build an in-memory pub\u002Fsub: topics, subscribers, message delivery. Use channels for delivery, goroutines for per-subscriber buffers, ",[18,954,746],{}," for unsubscription. Handle slow subscribers (buffered channels + drop or block policy).",[28,957,959],{"id":958},"_24-profiling-a-real-app-pprof","24. Profiling a Real App (pprof)",[14,961,962,963,966,967,970,971,974],{},"Build a server with ",[18,964,965],{},"net\u002Fhttp\u002Fpprof"," enabled. Load-test it (with ",[18,968,969],{},"hey"," or ",[18,972,973],{},"wrk","). Profile CPU and heap, find the hotspot, optimize (reduce allocations), re-profile. Document the before\u002Fafter.",[23,976,978],{"id":977},"exercise-find-the-bug","Exercise: Find the Bug",[14,980,981,982,985],{},"For each snippet, find the bug and write the fix. (Answers in ",[18,983,984],{},"\u003Cdetails>",".)",[28,987,989],{"id":988},"a-loop-variable-capture-pre-122","A. Loop variable capture (pre-1.22)",[48,991,992],{"language":50},[52,993,995],{"className":54,"code":994,"language":50,"meta":56,"style":56},"for i := 0; i \u003C 3; i++ {\n    go func() { fmt.Println(i) }()\n}\n",[18,996,997,1025,1042],{"__ignoreMap":56},[60,998,999,1001,1004,1006,1009,1012,1014,1017,1020,1023],{"class":62,"line":63},[60,1000,246],{"class":66},[60,1002,1003],{"class":87}," i ",[60,1005,413],{"class":66},[60,1007,1008],{"class":152}," 0",[60,1010,1011],{"class":87},"; i ",[60,1013,149],{"class":66},[60,1015,1016],{"class":152}," 3",[60,1018,1019],{"class":87},"; i",[60,1021,1022],{"class":66},"++",[60,1024,156],{"class":87},[60,1026,1027,1030,1033,1036,1039],{"class":62,"line":74},[60,1028,1029],{"class":66},"    go",[60,1031,1032],{"class":66}," func",[60,1034,1035],{"class":87},"() { fmt.",[60,1037,1038],{"class":70},"Println",[60,1040,1041],{"class":87},"(i) }()\n",[60,1043,1044],{"class":62,"line":81},[60,1045,236],{"class":87},[1047,1048,1049,1053],"details",{},[1050,1051,1052],"summary",{},"Answer",[14,1054,1055,1056,1059,1060,1063],{},"Pre-1.22, all goroutines see the final ",[18,1057,1058],{},"i"," (3, 3, 3) — the loop variable is shared. Fix: ",[18,1061,1062],{},"go func(i int) { fmt.Println(i) }(i)"," or update to Go 1.22+.",[28,1065,1067],{"id":1066},"b-nil-interface","B. Nil interface",[48,1069,1070],{"language":50},[52,1071,1073],{"className":54,"code":1072,"language":50,"meta":56,"style":56},"func f() error {\n    var p *MyError = nil\n    return p